# Keep the build context lean AND stable. Both the run-container builds
# (containers/*/Dockerfile, which compile the `draw`/`foray` binaries from
# crates/) and the service-image builds (deployments/images/*.Dockerfile, which
# compile the backend/auth/dispatcher/driver/artifacts/arena crates) use the
# repository root as their context. Every one of those builds is just a `cargo
# build` over the Rust workspace — nothing else — so this is an ALLOWLIST: ignore
# everything, then re-include only the paths cargo actually reads.
#
# Flipping to an allowlist (rather than enumerating things to exclude) means a
# change to anything cargo does NOT compile — the frontend, the docs, test cases,
# k8s manifests, models, this devcontainer — can never invalidate a build layer.
# Only a change to a file in the list below busts the `COPY . .` cache, which is
# the whole point: those edits genuinely shouldn't trigger an image rebuild.

# Ignore everything by default…
*

# …then re-include the Rust workspace and the few files a build embeds. All
# workspace members live under crates/, and no manifest reaches outside it, so
# this is the complete set cargo needs to resolve and compile any crate.
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/rust-toolchain.toml
!/.cargo
!/crates
# crates/core bakes these two trees into the binary verbatim via include_str!
# (the built-in orchestrator runner scripts and the harness manifests), so they
# must be present in the context even though they are not Rust sources.
!/orchestrators
!/harnesses

# The backend service image (deployments/images/backend.Dockerfile) bakes the
# Playwright browser-driver into its runtime to render references at ingest, so the
# driver script and its manifest must survive the allowlist too. (These are the one
# non-cargo exception above; editing either does bust the backend image's COPY
# cache, but they change very rarely.)
!/packages/browser-driver/package.json
!/packages/browser-driver/driver.mjs

# The adversarial and performance run-container images assemble a source-only
# "buildkit" — the verbatim engine crates plus a de-workspaced root Cargo.toml that
# re-supplies their `workspace = true` inheritance — which they `cp` from the build
# context and smoke-build standalone (see containers/{adversarial,performance}/Dockerfile).
# The crates ride in under !/crates, but these de-workspaced root manifests live
# outside it, so re-include them explicitly or the COPY/cp stages can't see them.
!/containers/adversarial/buildkit/Cargo.toml
!/containers/performance/buildkit/Cargo.toml

# The performance image bakes the committed training scenarios from the
# performance-factorio case's version folder (see containers/performance/Dockerfile's
# `COPY test-cases/.../references/training`). It is the one test-case tree a build
# embeds, so it must survive the allowlist; the path tracks the Dockerfile's COPY.
!/test-cases/performance-factorio/v1.0.0/references/training

# Re-exclude build outputs and scratch that can appear UNDER the re-included
# paths, so a local `cargo build`'s target/ (or a stray node_modules) never bloats
# the context or churns the layer cache. These come last so they win.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.astro/
